# headscale / vaultwarden warm standby

This directory holds the **stopped-by-default** standby containers for
headscale and vaultwarden. Do not run `docker compose up -d` here outside
a real failover -- follow the runbook:

    docs/runbooks/failover-headscale-vaultwarden.md

in the homelab-infrastructure repo.

## One-time manual prerequisites (not yet done by an automated role)

1. Copy these 3 files from the live headscale/vaultwarden pods to this host
   once (they rotate essentially never):
   - `{{ rpi_ha_standby_data_root }}/headscale/data/private.key`
   - `{{ rpi_ha_standby_data_root }}/headscale/data/noise_private.key`
   - `{{ rpi_ha_standby_data_root }}/vaultwarden/data/rsa_key.pem` (and
     `rsa_key.pub.pem`, `rsa_key.pem` alone regenerates the `.pub` on start)
2. Fill in `HEADSCALE_OIDC_CLIENT_SECRET` in
   `{{ rpi_ha_standby_compose_root }}/headscale/.env` (same value as the
   live `headscale-oidc` Kubernetes Secret).

Until both are done, `docker compose up -d` will still start both
containers, but headscale will mint a fresh node identity (breaking every
device's tailnet trust) and OIDC login won't work against the standby.
